    "created_at": "2024-07-04T18:07:49Z",
    "updated_at": "2024-07-04T18:07:49Z",
    "body": "In I18N's 2024-07-04 call, we talked about this issue. In general, we think that page author's would like to be able to control the appearance and localization of their pages. Having default controls such as submit, reset, etc. be localized (to the extent of the browser's capability) according to the `lang` of the node makes sense to use. The page author might be able to get default user-agent locale behavior by neutralizing the language (`lang=\"\"`)?\r\n",
